{"kind":"doc","route":"/guide/ai/","title":"AI agents","blocks":[{"t":"heading","level":1,"id":"ai-agents","children":[{"t":"text","text":"AI agents"}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"This section gathers everything that gives an AI agent access to CraftTS"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"knowledge, application state, runtime behavior, or debugging context."}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"There are three complementary layers:"}]},{"t":"list","ordered":true,"items":[[{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":""},{"t":"strong","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Knowledge"}]},{"t":"text","text":": documentation, examples, "},{"t":"code","text":"llms.txt"},{"t":"text","text":", and Agent Skills."}]}],[{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":""},{"t":"strong","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Observation and control"}]},{"t":"text","text":": MCP tools for the live browser, the runtime"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"registry, and application logs."}]}],[{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":""},{"t":"strong","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Application context"}]},{"t":"text","text":": "},{"t":"code","text":"provideSendContextToAi"},{"t":"text","text":", which lets a developer"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"assemble a selected screen, timeline, snapshot, and optional DOM/CSS capture"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"before copying or sending it to an AI service."}]}]]},{"t":"heading","level":2,"id":"choose-the-right-surface","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Choose the right surface"}]},{"t":"table","head":[[{"t":"text","text":"Need"}],[{"t":"text","text":"Start here"}],[{"t":"text","text":"Access"}]],"rows":[[[{"t":"text","text":"Learn CraftTS conventions or find an API"}],[{"t":"link","href":"/craft/resources/ai-agents","external":false,"children":[{"t":"text","text":"Coding agents"}]}],[{"t":"code","text":"@craft-ts/mcp"}]],[[{"t":"text","text":"Fill, click, navigate, or inspect the running app"}],[{"t":"link","href":"/craft/guide/ai/dev-page","external":false,"children":[{"t":"text","text":"Live page MCP"}]}],[{"t":"code","text":"@craft-ts/function-registry-mcp"},{"t":"text","text":" → "},{"t":"code","text":"page"}]],[[{"t":"text","text":"Read or change a published primitive during development"}],[{"t":"link","href":"/craft/guide/ai/mcp-tools","external":false,"children":[{"t":"text","text":"MCP tools"}]}],[{"t":"code","text":"registry.*"},{"t":"text","text":" tools"}]],[[{"t":"text","text":"Search logs from a reproducible flow"}],[{"t":"link","href":"/craft/guide/ai/mcp-tools","external":false,"children":[{"t":"text","text":"MCP tools"}]}],[{"t":"code","text":"@craft-ts/log-mcp"},{"t":"text","text":" → "},{"t":"code","text":"logs.*"}]],[[{"t":"text","text":"Ask what a node depends on, or what a change can break"}],[{"t":"link","href":"/craft/guide/ai/mcp-tools","external":false,"children":[{"t":"text","text":"MCP tools"}]}],[{"t":"code","text":"@craft-ts/graph-mcp"},{"t":"text","text":" → "},{"t":"code","text":"graph.*"}]],[[{"t":"text","text":"Export, share, or replay a debugging session"}],[{"t":"link","href":"/craft/guide/ai/send-context-webhook","external":false,"children":[{"t":"text","text":"Send context to AI"}]}],[{"t":"code","text":"provideSendContextToAi"}]],[[{"t":"text","text":"Understand the tracing and snapshot data behind the context"}],[{"t":"link","href":"/craft/guide/advanced/observability","external":false,"children":[{"t":"text","text":"Observability"}]}],[{"t":"text","text":"Craft providers and runtime hooks"}]]]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"The tools are deliberately separated by boundary. The documentation MCP is"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"read-only and works offline. The registry MCP can mutate development state and"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"must only be connected to a local development app. The logs MCP reads local"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"JSONL files; its "},{"t":"code","text":"logs.clear"},{"t":"text","text":" operation is destructive. The graph MCP reads the"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"static dependency graph of the project and only writes the graph file it"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"rebuilds."}]},{"t":"heading","level":2,"id":"mcp-servers","children":[{"t":"text","text":"MCP servers"}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"CraftTS has four MCP servers, each with a different responsibility:"}]},{"t":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"link","href":"https://www.npmjs.com/package/@craft-ts/mcp","external":true,"children":[{"t":"code","text":"@craft-ts/mcp"}]},{"t":"text","text":" gives an agent"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"the published documentation, examples, skills, and LLM entry points."}]}],[{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"link","href":"/craft/guide/ai/mcp-tools","external":false,"children":[{"t":"code","text":"@craft-ts/function-registry-mcp"}]},{"t":"text","text":" bridges a running"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"browser tab to "},{"t":"code","text":"page"},{"t":"text","text":" and "},{"t":"code","text":"registry.*"},{"t":"text","text":" tools."}]}],[{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"link","href":"/craft/guide/ai/mcp-tools","external":false,"children":[{"t":"code","text":"@craft-ts/log-mcp"}]},{"t":"text","text":" exposes the local log store through"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"code","text":"logs.*"},{"t":"text","text":" tools."}]}],[{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"link","href":"/craft/guide/ai/mcp-tools","external":false,"children":[{"t":"code","text":"@craft-ts/graph-mcp"}]},{"t":"text","text":" answers architecture questions"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"from the static dependency graph through "},{"t":"code","text":"graph.*"},{"t":"text","text":" tools."}]}]]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"See "},{"t":"link","href":"/craft/guide/ai/mcp-tools","external":false,"children":[{"t":"text","text":"MCP tools"}]},{"t":"text","text":" for the complete tool inventory and the"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"boundary between read-only and mutating operations."}]},{"t":"heading","level":2,"id":"context-integrations","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Context integrations"}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"This section is also the home for context providers and future agent-facing"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"integrations. "},{"t":"code","text":"provideSendContextToAi"},{"t":"text","text":" is the first application-facing context"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"surface: it turns an interaction into structured context that can be copied or"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"sent to a protected webhook."}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Lucene and Context Workbook are not present as packages, tools, or documented"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"integrations in this repository yet. When they are introduced, their setup,"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"permissions, context model, and MCP tools should be documented under this"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"section and added to the table above rather than creating another AI-related"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"navigation branch."}]}],"outline":[{"level":2,"id":"choose-the-right-surface","text":"Choose the right surface"},{"level":2,"id":"mcp-servers","text":"MCP servers"},{"level":2,"id":"context-integrations","text":"Context integrations"}]}